.TH 7ZIPLX 1 "2026-11-23" "7zipLX 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
7ziplx \- native Linux GUI for the 7-Zip archive engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 7ziplx
.RI [ archive ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 7ziplx
is a single-pane archive manager with an optional second pane (F9), built with
Qt 6. It uses the portable 7-Zip engine for archive formats, compression,
extraction, testing, hashing and archive editing.
.PP
When
.I archive
is given, it is opened in the active panel after startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the application version.
.TP
.B \-\-extract-here
Extract each positional archive into its own folder and exit without opening
the main window.
.TP
.BI \-\-extract-to " directory"
Extract the positional archives into \fIdirectory\fR and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-compress
Compress each positional file or folder to a sibling \fIname\fR.7z archive and
exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-compress-to " archive"
Compress all positional paths into \fIarchive\fR and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Do not ask before replacing an existing archive in command-line mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/7zipLX/7zipLX.conf
Persisted window, panel and tool settings.
.TP
.I /usr/share/7ziplx/translations
Optional compiled Qt translation catalogs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 7z (1),
.BR 7zz (1)
.SH AUTHOR
7zipLX contributors.
